### Phase 2: Planning Flow API Requests
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/v1
@roomId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@ideaId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002

### 1. BRIEF ENDPOINTS

### 1.1 Get Brief
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/brief
Content-Type: application/json

### 1.2 Save Brief (Manual or Draft)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/brief
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "source": "manual",
  "sourceUrl": null,
  "fileName": null,
  "rawText": "Manual brief content",
  "fields": {
    "problemStatement": "Teams struggle to coordinate hackathon delivery in 36 hours.",
    "targetAudience": "Hackathon participants and mentors",
    "rubric": [
      { "criterion": "Innovation", "weight": 30 },
      { "criterion": "Technical Architecture", "weight": 40 },
      { "criterion": "Demo Polish", "weight": 30 }
    ],
    "deadlines": {
      "start": "2026-10-15T09:00:00Z",
      "freeze": "2026-10-16T18:00:00Z",
      "submission": "2026-10-16T21:00:00Z"
    },
    "eligibility": "University students and professionals",
    "techRules": "Open source libraries allowed",
    "aiPolicy": "AI coding tools encouraged with disclosure",
    "deliverables": ["Live demo", "GitHub repository"],
    "tracksAndPrizes": ["Open innovation ($5000)"],
    "judgingFormat": "3 minute live pitch"
  },
  "confirmedFields": {},
  "risks": ["Time crunch", "Scope creep"]
}

### 1.3 Update Confirmed Field
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/brief/confirmed-fields
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fieldKey": "problemStatement",
  "confirmed": true
}

### 1.4 Set Link Source (SSRF guarded)
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/brief/source/link
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://example.com/hackathon"
}

### 1.5 Get Extraction Prompt
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/brief/extraction-prompt

### 1.6 Validate Extracted JSON
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/brief/extract/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jsonText": "{\"problemStatement\":\"Test\",\"targetAudience\":\"Students\",\"rubric\":[{\"criterion\":\"Execution\",\"weight\":100}],\"deadlines\":{\"start\":null,\"freeze\":null,\"submission\":null}}"
}

### 1.7 Auto Extract via AI
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/brief/extract/auto

### 1.8 Confirm Brief (Advances stage to ideate)
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/brief/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "applyDatesToRoom": true
}

### 1.9 Delete / Reset Brief
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/brief


### 2. IDEAS ENDPOINTS

### 2.1 Get Ideate Overview
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/ideate

### 2.2 List Ideas
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/ideas

### 2.3 Post Idea
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/ideas
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "A real-time opinionated OS guiding hackathon teams from rules to pitch with prompt chaining.",
  "links": [
    { "url": "https://github.com", "title": "GitHub" }
  ],
  "notes": ["Focus on sprint time limits"]
}

### 2.4 Update Idea (Author only, pending only)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/ideas/{{ideaId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "Updated text for the hackathon idea proposition.",
  "links": [],
  "notes": []
}

### 2.5 Delete Idea (Author only, pending only)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/ideas/{{ideaId}}

### 2.6 Approve Idea (Leader only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/ideas/{{ideaId}}/approve

### 2.7 Reject Idea (Leader only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/ideas/{{ideaId}}/reject
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Scope too broad for a 36-hour sprint"
}

### 2.8 Restore Idea (Undo rejection)
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/ideas/{{ideaId}}/restore

### 2.9 Set Primary Pitch Idea (Single star rule)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/ideas/{{ideaId}}/primary

### 2.10 Clear Primary Idea
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/ideas/{{ideaId}}/primary

### 2.11 Mark Ideation Done (Requires at least 1 approved idea)
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/ideation/done

### 2.12 Reopen Ideation
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/ideation/reopen

### 2.13 Export Ideas Markdown
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/ideas/export.md

### 2.14 Dev Seed Sample Ideas
POST {{baseUrl}}/dev/rooms/{{roomId}}/seed-ideas


### 3. PLAN ENDPOINTS

### 3.1 Get Plan State & Steps
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/plan

### 3.2 Save Step Draft (800ms autosave)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/plan/steps/prd
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "answer": "# PRD\n## Problem\nProblem description\n## Target user\nUsers\n## One-sentence identity\nIdentity\n## Core flow\n1. Step 1\n2. Step 2\n3. Step 3\n## Wow moment\nWow\n## Must-have features\nFeatures\n## Out of scope\nOut\n# MVP\n## The one end-to-end flow\nFlow\n## Real vs mocked\n| Part | Status |\n|---|---|\n| API | Real |\n## Cut list\n- Cut 1\n- Cut 2\n- Cut 3\n## Risks and fallbacks\nRisks",
  "confirmClear": false
}

### 3.3 Validate Step (Enforces step order prd -> tech -> phases -> tasks -> demo)
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/plan/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stepKey": "prd",
  "answer": "# PRD\n## Problem\nProblem description\n## Target user\nUsers\n## One-sentence identity\nIdentity\n## Core flow\n1. Step 1\n2. Step 2\n3. Step 3\n## Wow moment\nWow\n## Must-have features\nFeatures\n## Out of scope\nOut\n# MVP\n## The one end-to-end flow\nFlow\n## Real vs mocked\n| Part | Status |\n|---|---|\n| API | Real |\n## Cut list\n- Cut 1\n- Cut 2\n- Cut 3\n## Risks and fallbacks\nRisks"
}

### 3.4 AI Generate Step
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/plan/steps/prd/generate

### 3.5 Download Context Pack Markdown
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/plan/context.md?step=prd

### 3.6 Enter Build Phase (Stage advances to build, locks plan)
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/stage/enter-build

### 3.7 Unlock Build Early (Leader skip plan)
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/stage/unlock-build


### 4. MINIMAL READ ENDPOINTS (DOCS & BOARD)

### 4.1 List Generated Documents
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/docs

### 4.2 Get Document Detail Content
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/docs/PRD.md

### 4.3 Get Board Kanban Columns and Members
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/board
